 "wiki": {
  "lang": "en",
  "title": "Pin-tailed sandgrouse",
  "extract": "The pin-tailed sandgrouse is a medium large bird in the sandgrouse family. It has a small, pigeon-like head and neck and a sturdy, compact body. It has long pointed wings, which are white underneath, a long tail and a fast direct flight. Flocks fly to watering holes at dawn. The call is a loud kattar-kattar. This gregarious species breeds on dry open treeless plains and similar habitats. Its nest is a ground scrape into which two or three cream-coloured eggs with cryptic markings are laid. Both sexes incubate the eggs.",
  "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pin-tailed_sandgrouse"
 },
